# Documentation

A feature is not done until its docs match the code, updated in the same change (same commit, or a `docs:` commit right after it). Write for an agent that never saw this conversation: record what the code cannot tell.

## One home per fact

Each fact lives in one doc; others link to it instead of copying.

| Doc | Holds | Update when |
|---|---|---|
| `internal/<module>/README.md` | module context (template below) | module behavior, files, flags, invariants change |
| `ARCHITECTURE.md` | map: binaries, modules, topics, HTTP contracts, boundaries, invariants | a module, binary, topic, table or contract is added or changed |
| `AGENTS.md` | commands, conventions, docs index | commands, env vars or workflow change |
| `README.md` (Portuguese, for humans) | what the project is, how to run it | setup, commands, structure or ports change |
| `docs/decisions/NNNN-title.md` | ADR | a choice that is expensive to reverse |

Platform packages (`internal/config`, `internal/platform/*`) only need Go doc comments, not a README.

## Module README

English, short (aim for under 80 lines). Sections: `Purpose`, `Entry points`, `Flow`, `Key files`, `Invariants and gotchas`, `Configuration`, `Testing`, `Update when`. See `internal/simulator/README.md`.

## ADRs

- Write one when a future reader would pay to rediscover why: new dependency, contract shape, delivery semantics, storage, cross-module convention.
- Copy `docs/decisions/_template.md` with the next number and add it to `docs/decisions/README.md`.
- Accepted ADRs are never rewritten: add a new ADR and mark the old one `Superseded by NNNN`.

## What to write

- Do: invariants, boundaries, why something odd is odd, exact paths, commands, flags and env vars.
- Do not: file listings or signatures readable from code, session notes, TODO logs, credentials.
- Mark things that do not exist yet as **planned**.

## Before finishing

1. Check each row of the table above against the change and update what it touches.
2. Remove statements the change made false.
3. Verify every path and command mentioned in touched docs still exists and works.
